Name the kext whose load is entered

start() has enter and leave now, and run-272's panel ends on a load-succeeded
line with every start> closed, which puts the stall inside a load.  Print the
identifier on the way into load() as well; the dependency walk that pulls in apfs
and zlib is exactly the stretch that has no kext id line of its own.
---
diff --git a/libkern/c++/OSKext.cpp b/libkern/c++/OSKext.cpp
index d14d5c1..ecc7fcf 100644
--- a/libkern/c++/OSKext.cpp
+++ b/libkern/c++/OSKext.cpp
@@ -6304,6 +6304,13 @@ OSKext::load(
 	OSArray            * personalityNames)
 {
 	OSReturn             result                       = kOSReturnError;
+
+	/* nio: start() is bracketed now, load() is not.  run-272 ends on a "load
+	 * succeeded" line with every start> closed, so the next stall is inside a
+	 * load -- most likely the dependency walk that loads apfs and zlib.  One
+	 * line in and one line out names it, the same way start> did. */
+	printf("nio: load> %s\n",
+	    (getIdentifierCString() != NULL) ? getIdentifierCString() : "(null)");
 	OSKextExcludeLevel   dependenciesStartOpt         = startOpt;
 	OSKextExcludeLevel   dependenciesStartMatchingOpt = startMatchingOpt;
 	unsigned int         i, count;
